Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report houji's missing battery times as no data

Houji's battery firmware reports time_to_empty_avg and time_to_full_avg
as 0 while it discharges or charges; the estimate is made by the stock
Android framework, not the firmware. A 0 reads as "empty now": Armada's
MangoHud shows 00:00 remaining. Return -ENODATA for a 0 on houji, so
readers fall back to their own estimate, as UPower already does.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -706,9 +706,16 @@
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.soh_percent;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_EMPTY_AVG:
+		/* Houji's firmware reports 0 when it has no estimate. */
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_XIAOMI_HOUJI &&
+		    !battmgr->status.discharge_time)
+			return -ENODATA;
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.discharge_time;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_FULL_AVG:
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_XIAOMI_HOUJI &&
+		    !battmgr->status.charge_time)
+			return -ENODATA;
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.charge_time;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_CONTROL_START_THRESHOLD:
